# Python bytecode.
#
# These were tracked until now, and it cost real friction: the caches are
# regenerated by every run, so they showed up as spurious modifications in
# unrelated commits, and any cleanup of a working tree deleted tracked files
# that then had to be restored. They are also interpreter-specific -- this repo
# accumulated a mix of cpython-312 (the GPU box) and cpython-314 (the Windows
# workstation) for the same modules, so neither copy was authoritative and both
# went stale whenever either interpreter moved a minor version.
#
# Nothing depended on them. Two orphans at the repo root,
# helper_functions*.pyc, outlived their sources, but those sources are still in
# history (git show 41ff6cf:helper_functions.py) and the only importer,
# obsolete/deeponet.py, could not have worked from them anyway: Python does not
# import a sourceless .pyc that sits in __pycache__/.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
